# unfocused-pacing.xrs - the session-33 regression, on a desk.
#
# Losing FOCUSED is what collapsed the frame rate in session 33. The sim can
# command that transition, so the bug is a repeatable test instead of an
# accident that needed a headset to reproduce.
#
# The oracle is the FRAME RATE, not the session state: a state field cannot tell
# you the game got slow. @fps fails the run if submission stalls while unfocused.
#
# SCOPE, and it matters: this measures the MOD's pacing against the SIM's model
# of focus loss (the sim keeps delivering frames while VISIBLE, which is
# spec-correct). It does NOT prove VDXR behaves the same. A pass here means the
# mod's own pacing path survives losing focus; the hardware question stays open.
reset
@frames 30
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@fps 60
focus lose
@wait 2000
@assert sessionState eq VISIBLE
# The real check: frames must keep flowing while unfocused.
@fps 60
focus regain
@wait 2000
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@fps 60
